-- Rules that start two copies of themselves at once, beside rules with the
-- same RAND that start themselves only once, which draw no warning. Recursion-limit
-- ruling L3 (2026-11-20) asks for a positive and a
-- negative fixture for each shape a warning fires on, and ruling L4 says that
-- @ends-because never silences this warning. Both are described in
-- doc/reference/regulative/rules-that-start-themselves-again.md, and the
-- golden pins the text of each message.
--
-- A marked rule here never follows one that draws this warning: after a
-- comment, an annotation is counted into the range of the expression before
-- it, which would stretch that warning down to the mark.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alex, Sam
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF `pay rent`, `pay a fee`

-- Warns: the mark answers "could not check" (the deadline is counted from a
-- fixed moment), and that warning is gone, but not this one.
@ends-because Alex pays before day 2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`fixed chaser` MEANS
    PARTY Alex
    MUST `pay rent`
    WITHIN 1 OF 2
    LEST (`fixed chaser` RAND `fixed chaser`)

-- Warns: every time the deadline is missed, the number of copies open doubles.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`chaser` MEANS
    PARTY Alex
    MUST `pay rent`
    WITHIN 7
    LEST (`chaser` RAND `chaser`)

-- No warning: the RAND joins one new copy of the rule with a different duty.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`late fee` MEANS
    PARTY Alex
    MUST `pay a fee`
    WITHIN 14

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`fee and reminder` MEANS
    PARTY Alex
    MUST `pay rent`
    WITHIN 7
    LEST (`late fee` RAND `fee and reminder`)

-- Warns on `second chaser`, whose LEST starts the copies, and names the rules
-- that lead back to each other on a line of their own. The mark above `first
-- chaser` does not silence it.
@ends-because Alex pays in the end
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`first chaser` MEANS
    PARTY Alex
    MUST `pay rent`
    WITHIN 7
    LEST `second chaser`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`second chaser` MEANS
    PARTY Sam
    MUST `pay rent`
    WITHIN 7
    LEST (`first chaser` RAND `first chaser`)

-- Warns, and says how far it can grow: `n` drops by 1 at each step down.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`spreading chaser` n MEANS
    IF n EQUALS 0
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY Alex
         MUST `pay rent`
         WITHIN 7
         LEST (`spreading chaser` (n MINUS 1) RAND `spreading chaser` (n MINUS 1))

-- Warns, and says how far it can grow when `n` drops by 2 at each step down.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`faster chaser` n MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY Alex
         MUST `pay rent`
         WITHIN 7
         LEST (`faster chaser` (n MINUS 2) RAND `faster chaser` (n MINUS 2))
